        <type>double</type>
        <definition>double Assembly::Elasticity::enlarged_mesh_forcing_lobe_peak</definition>
        <argsstring>(const double gamma, const double exponent)</argsstring>
        <name>enlarged_mesh_forcing_lobe_peak</name>
        <qualifiedname>Assembly::Elasticity::enlarged_mesh_forcing_lobe_peak</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const double</type>
          <declname>gamma</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const double</type>
          <declname>exponent</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Peak of the dimensionless enlarged-compression lobe associated with the one-dimensional Helmholtz marker. Away from the much thinner physical interface, psi - L^2 psi&apos;&apos; = sign(x) gives</para>
<para>L |grad psi| = 1 - |psi|.</para>
<para>Hence the lobe shape, with s = |psi| in [0,1], is</para>
<para>(1-s) |factor(equalize_q(s))|.</para>
<para>A short, deterministic one-dimensional search is sufficient here. Its result is stored by the forcing assembler and reused in all FE loops. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
